<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 31.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 31.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 01/31/97  01/24/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     83.31    103.61    35.83	44.55     26.1</p>
<p>West	     79.09     93.98    30.52	36.27     38.2</p>
<p>Total Canada  162.40    197.58    33.03	40.19     32.5</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 01/31/97: 232.55 bcf, 01/24/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 01/31/97: 259.11 bcf, 01/24/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
